WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.790
What happened?

3
00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:13.910
What the fuck do we do now. Manuel?
The whole Army will be on our ass!

4
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.310
- God has already shown me the way.
- And what is this fucking way?

5
00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.230
Why don't you wait for me upstairs?

6
00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:56.190
- I'll be right up with a drink.
- Yeah.

7
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.110
How old is she?

8
00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.510
You're all over the news. asshole.

9
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:30.030
The shipment left safe and sound.

10
00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.470
I did my job.

11
00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.230
What do you want?

12
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:38.670
A meeting with the Leyras.

13
00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:42.110
You're too hot to go near them now.

14
00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:47.390
It's not a question.

15
00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:01.870
What's all this?
You think I give a shit about her?

16
00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:10.350
Kill her.
Kill her. motherfucker. Go on!

17
00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.510
I think you're misunderstanding
our presence here.

18
00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:20.270
You're a dead man. asshole.
You and all your shitbag men. Get it?

19
00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.470
How do you think we got in?

20
00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:28.030
By politely asking your goons
if we could have a chat with you?

21
00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:35.070
Mexico trained us to be the best.
And we are.

22
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.150
That's why I want to suggest

23
00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:44.350
you make life easier
for your bosses. the Leyras.

24
00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.270
or make it more difficult for them.

25
00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.750
Why don't you cut the bullshit

26
00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.990
and tell me what the fuck
you're doing in my house?

27
00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:58.510
I already told you. a meeting.

28
00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.070
Or else?

29
00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:04.750
Or else...

30
00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.350
I'll boil you alive.

31
00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.190
Starting with your feet

32
00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:13.550
and when they're cooked.

33
00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.830
I'll cut them off

34
00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:20.470
and I'll keep you alive
so you can eat them.

35
00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.430
right down to the toenails.

36
00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.630
What do you say?

37
00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:39.150
- Hello. Chief. Who are these guys?
- They came to see the boss.

38
00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:41.190
Open up. motherfucker.

39
00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:43.910
Open up.

40
00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.870
God has told me that our future
lies in your organization.

41
00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:20.230
You can tell your God that a bunch
of ex-soldiers don't do me any good.

42
00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:24.510
We don't see things
from the same perspective. sir.

43
00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:28.790
What perspective
are you talking about. Manuel?

44
00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:33.470
You aren't taking advantage
of your dominance in the marketplace.

45
00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:37.270
You keep selling wholesale
when you could be selling retail.

46
00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:43.590
So you're suggesting
to pay the dealers on every street?

47
00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.630
That's impossible.

48
00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:50.310
You don't have to pay them.
you just have to control them.

49
00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:53.470
And that's our expertise.

50
00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.590
And you need all these men for this?

51
00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.270
Who is the least skilled?

52
00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:11.190
- We're all skilled.
- I didn't ask that. The least skilled...

53
00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:16.910
One. two. three...

54
00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:20.550
I'll pick four.

55
00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.590
The fifth... we'll kill him.

56
00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:31.550
Well. I say... we'll kill this one.

57
00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:36.110
This little shit. okay?
But I don't know. you decide.

58
00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:43.310
What?
We need men who obey.

59
00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:48.710
- You need loyal men.
- Loyal to us. asshole! Come on.

60
00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:53.310
- Easy!
- Shoot. asshole. shoot!

61
00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:57.190
I'll wipe out everyone
you've ever known!

62
00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.190
Jacinto...

63
00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.990
We came here to work.

64
00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:05.910
All of us.

65
00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:11.270
God wants it this way.

66
00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.390
Let's talk. Manuel.

67
00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:21.230
ZEROZEROZERO

68
00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:30.750
THE ALTLANTIC OCEAN

69
00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:34.270
There's no way we can take the ship
to Gioia Tauro.

70
00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:37.790
Our best bet is to do
what the Mexican said.

71
00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:42.030
Trans-ship in the port of Dakar.
get a clean boat and finish that way.

72
00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:46.710
Until then. we shut down AIS and
INMARSAT and we stay out of sight.

73
00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:49.990
Okay.

74
00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.030
Chart a course for Senegal.

75
00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:57.630
Sounders. I want full speed.
all the way there.

76
00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.630
- Add whatever watches you need.
- Yes. sir.

77
00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:10.030
I was boarded by pirates once.

78
00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:17.750
It was many years ago.
when your father still liked to sail.

79
00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.790
Six of them boarded.
held us at gunpoint.

80
00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:27.150
Your father was a tougher man
than anyone had ever met. but...

81
00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:31.190
when you have a rifle
between the eyes...

82
00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:38.630
There is no such thing
as a hero at sea.

83
00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:21.310
- Mister Lynwood. can I help you?
- I just want to see it in action.

84
00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:24.390
- You need ear protection.
- I know.

85
00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:06.950
I was just in the aux engine room.
And I noticed there was oil everywhere.

86
00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:10.510
And I went over to the cylinders.

87
00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:14.190
And they were loose.
they were pouring oil.

88
00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:17.070
I'm sure somebody just missed it
on the maintenance check.

89
00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:19.710
No. every single one of the filters
was loose.

90
00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:22.910
If we hit rough waters.
started up those engines

91
00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:24.830
there'd be a fire in ten minutes.

92
00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:27.630
I know what I am talking about.
you know that.

93
00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:29.630
I grew up on your boats.

94
00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:32.950
I tend not to assume malice
when stupidity's on the table.

95
00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:35.750
They didn't just loosen themselves.

96
00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:42.550
Don't worry. I've been working
with those guys for many years.

97
00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:45.830
Your father knows them.

98
00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:49.070
All of them.

99
00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:01.190
Luzvimino. right?

100
00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:04.430
- You work in the oil room?
- Yes. sir.

101
00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:23.590
Nice boat. isn't it?

102
00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:25.950
We thought about going
with a two-stroke.

103
00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:30.630
but after looking at the start-up cost
we decided to go with this one.

104
00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:34.870
Do you need something.
Mr. Lynwood?

105
00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.990
Why are you trying
to start an engine fire?

106
00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.150
What do you mean?

107
00:18:57.390 --> 00:19:01.270
I have you on tape unscrewing the oil
cylinders on one of the aux engines.

108
00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:05.590
- I don't know what you're talking about.
- Don't fuck with me!

109
00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:10.910
I need you to tell me
what the fuck is going on.

110
00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:16.230
Why are you trying
to burn down my ship?

111
00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:22.150
He told me to do it. I'm sorry. pal.
I'm sorry. sir. I'm sorry.

112
00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:24.990
Who told you?

113
00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:27.470
Who the fuck told you?

114
00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:32.590
The Chief engineer.

115
00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:42.430
Have you talked
to anyone about this?

116
00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:45.190
No. I came straight to you.
but we need to call Emma.

117
00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:47.950
No!
It's too dangerous.

118
00:19:48.150 --> 00:19:50.550
Anything with the transmitter
stays off until we unload.

119
00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:53.230
- I need to tell her what's going on.
- You don't need to tell her anything.

120
00:21:02.670 --> 00:21:04.030
Fuck.

121
00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:06.310
Fuck! Help!
Fuck!

122
00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:26.630
Fuck!

123
00:25:58.590 --> 00:26:01.990
NEW ORLEANS. U.S.A.

124
00:26:42.350 --> 00:26:43.830
You need a ride home.

125
00:26:56.230 --> 00:26:58.750
How long have you been doing
this work?

126
00:27:01.910 --> 00:27:03.310
Since I was 20.

127
00:27:06.790 --> 00:27:08.110
I love the sea.

128
00:27:08.550 --> 00:27:12.670
You can see the Strait of Messina
from my window.

129
00:27:14.910 --> 00:27:16.790
I hate the sea.

130
00:27:20.310 --> 00:27:23.910
I hate these new mega ships
that sail on their own.

131
00:27:24.110 --> 00:27:29.710
the Filipino crews paid peanuts
who don't even know what the sea is.

132
00:27:31.470 --> 00:27:37.630
It wasn't like that before.
When I started. it was all different.

133
00:27:38.910 --> 00:27:40.630
Turn right. here.

134
00:27:57.390 --> 00:27:58.950
Why don't you quit?

135
00:27:59.990 --> 00:28:02.230
- What else could I do?
- Enjoy life.

136
00:28:06.590 --> 00:28:09.870
We can get you 100.000 dollars
the day after tomorrow.

137
00:28:10.990 --> 00:28:14.350
And a million euros when it's done.
wherever you want.

138
00:28:21.150 --> 00:28:22.430
What do you want?

139
00:28:23.390 --> 00:28:27.310
We want to be sure the shipment
never gets to Gioia Tauro.

140
00:28:34.030 --> 00:28:36.230
- How?
- I don't care how.

141
00:28:38.590 --> 00:28:42.030
What matters is that no one
ever knows it was you or us.

142
00:28:45.190 --> 00:28:48.990
- Edward Lynwood was my friend.
- Now he's dead.

143
00:28:53.550 --> 00:28:54.950
Right?

144
00:29:03.870 --> 00:29:08.830
REGGIO CALABRIA. ITALY

145
00:29:16.230 --> 00:29:18.630
What's your brother's wife
doing here?

146
00:29:18.790 --> 00:29:20.110
Where's Nicola?

147
00:29:20.190 --> 00:29:23.390
- He was supposed to meet us.
- Your brother didn't come home.

148
00:29:23.590 --> 00:29:26.990
He's been missing since yesterday.
he's not answering his phone.

149
00:29:27.190 --> 00:29:30.070
He had to see a guy.
but I don't know who.

150
00:29:31.270 --> 00:29:32.670
Come with Uncle.

151
00:29:34.190 --> 00:29:36.390
It's your fuckin' grandfather.

152
00:30:42.310 --> 00:30:44.190
What a lovely parmigiana!

153
00:30:46.990 --> 00:30:48.430
The American's back.

154
00:30:48.790 --> 00:30:50.430
Where is he?

155
00:30:52.030 --> 00:30:53.470
Where is he?

156
00:30:57.830 --> 00:31:01.870
- Look how you've grown!
- My knees reach your shoulders.

157
00:31:01.990 --> 00:31:06.270
- Tell me how much you missed Daddy.
- This much.

158
00:31:07.070 --> 00:31:09.630
- Do you know how much I missed you?
- No.

159
00:31:10.350 --> 00:31:11.990
This much!

160
00:31:15.550 --> 00:31:16.670
Go with Mommy.

161
00:32:15.710 --> 00:32:18.390
Don't worry. we'll fix this.

162
00:32:19.670 --> 00:32:22.590
You've always fixed everything.
Remember that.

163
00:32:23.430 --> 00:32:27.190
Daddy. wanna come play with my truck?

164
00:32:28.270 --> 00:32:31.070
Yes. you go to the living room.
I'll be right there.

165
00:32:41.790 --> 00:32:43.830
Your grandfather wants you.

166
00:32:45.870 --> 00:32:47.470
He wants to speak to you.

167
00:32:49.510 --> 00:32:51.030
I'll see you tonight.

168
00:32:54.150 --> 00:32:56.390
Yes. will you put your son to bed?

169
00:32:57.510 --> 00:32:58.750
Get my jacket.

170
00:35:09.790 --> 00:35:12.270
Hi. Stefano.
Sit down.

171
00:35:26.590 --> 00:35:28.150
You must be hungry.

172
00:35:29.430 --> 00:35:30.790
Eat something.

173
00:35:47.990 --> 00:35:50.950
How come you didn't tell me
about America?

174
00:35:53.710 --> 00:35:57.390
You had the cops on your ass
and your contact was dead.

175
00:35:58.670 --> 00:36:02.710
So you tried to take the shipment away
from Emma Lynwood?

176
00:36:03.590 --> 00:36:07.110
I went to offer my condolences.
and get to know them.

177
00:36:08.150 --> 00:36:10.750
The boy let the girl boss him around.

178
00:36:12.470 --> 00:36:14.790
You put important stuff in her hands.

179
00:36:15.470 --> 00:36:19.350
In my opinion they're a couple of fools
with no experience.

180
00:36:20.870 --> 00:36:22.430
Edward's daughter...

181
00:36:22.990 --> 00:36:26.190
I saw her baptized
thirty years ago in America.

182
00:36:28.550 --> 00:36:31.470
I know more than you.

183
00:36:35.750 --> 00:36:38.830
I made a mistake
thinking I was doing right. Grandpa.

184
00:38:21.830 --> 00:38:24.230
- Welcome. Don Minu.
- Benedetto.

185
00:38:24.310 --> 00:38:25.670
Good to see you.

186
00:38:29.350 --> 00:38:30.670
Thank you.

187
00:38:52.190 --> 00:38:53.230
She's ready. Dad.

188
00:39:15.390 --> 00:39:16.390
Here.

189
00:39:22.070 --> 00:39:23.350
Come here!

190
00:39:30.270 --> 00:39:31.510
What's wrong?

191
00:39:32.750 --> 00:39:34.030
Come here!

192
00:39:35.750 --> 00:39:37.390
Hold her still.

193
00:41:47.310 --> 00:41:51.990
What happened to the courier
has put all the families on edge.

194
00:41:53.710 --> 00:41:55.470
The shipment is in transit.

195
00:41:56.270 --> 00:41:59.110
And they haven't asked us
for an extra cent.

196
00:41:59.550 --> 00:42:02.950
The shipment will arrive.
everyone can put their mind at ease.

197
00:42:04.510 --> 00:42:06.150
And if it doesn't arrive?

198
00:42:08.430 --> 00:42:10.150
Then my enemies win

199
00:42:10.990 --> 00:42:14.470
and I die with all those
who are still loyal to me.

200
00:42:17.230 --> 00:42:18.630
This will be few.

201
00:42:20.150 --> 00:42:21.430
Very few.

202
00:42:29.270 --> 00:42:33.350
Don Minu... I've been wanting to talk
to you for a long time.

203
00:42:34.310 --> 00:42:35.710
Then talk.

204
00:42:38.790 --> 00:42:40.310
My son...

205
00:42:41.630 --> 00:42:43.990
took care of a rival.

206
00:42:46.310 --> 00:42:48.870
And now the guy's mother
is asking around.

207
00:42:50.670 --> 00:42:53.990
If we don't tell her what happened.
she'll go to the cops.

208
00:42:56.990 --> 00:43:00.190
Does she know her son is dead?

209
00:43:01.110 --> 00:43:02.390
Yes.

210
00:43:02.990 --> 00:43:06.110
- And that your son killed him?
- Yes. she knows.

211
00:43:10.590 --> 00:43:12.270
She wants to bury him.

212
00:43:12.830 --> 00:43:16.910
With all due respect. Don Minu.
we know what we have to do.

213
00:43:17.590 --> 00:43:20.550
That woman has to be buried
together with her son.

214
00:43:20.870 --> 00:43:24.230
If you'll allow it.
I'll do the job personally.

215
00:43:26.830 --> 00:43:30.550
Women and children
are never to be touched.

216
00:43:35.550 --> 00:43:40.070
Tell people
that when they hear about her son.

217
00:43:40.990 --> 00:43:42.710
they ignore her

218
00:43:43.510 --> 00:43:45.630
and turn away.

219
00:44:01.550 --> 00:44:03.590
Do you mind if I use the bathroom?

220
00:44:05.230 --> 00:44:06.430
Please.

221
00:44:39.750 --> 00:44:40.950
Where are you?

222
00:44:42.990 --> 00:44:44.430
Page 39.

223
00:45:08.870 --> 00:45:11.790
Italo. it's Lucia.
I spoke to Stefano.

224
00:45:12.590 --> 00:45:14.670
They are at Bellantone's house.

225
00:45:30.870 --> 00:45:34.150
Thank you. everybody.
We have to go now.

226
00:45:35.430 --> 00:45:38.910
- You're always welcome. Don Minu.
- Grandpa. it's getting late.

227
00:45:39.550 --> 00:45:43.670
I'm sure Don Benedetto's happy
to put you up for the night.

228
00:45:47.070 --> 00:45:51.190
I've got a place for you. out back.
There's everything you need.

229
00:45:52.790 --> 00:45:54.790
Thanks a lot. Benedetto.

230
00:45:56.550 --> 00:46:00.670
But I need to take my grandson
somewhere else.

231
00:46:01.070 --> 00:46:02.670
Say goodbye. Stefano.

232
00:46:06.630 --> 00:46:09.470
I might come back later tonight.
Benedetto.

233
00:46:18.830 --> 00:46:20.070
Give it to me.

234
00:46:24.550 --> 00:46:28.070
- What?
- Give it to me. don't make me ask again.

235
00:47:34.470 --> 00:47:36.870
You know why the last war started?

236
00:47:38.630 --> 00:47:41.830
They attacked you.
And my father fought back.

237
00:47:44.950 --> 00:47:46.750
That's what they say.

238
00:47:49.990 --> 00:47:51.510
But that's not true.

239
00:47:52.790 --> 00:47:57.190
Your father and Gianni Curtiga
attacked first.

240
00:47:59.230 --> 00:48:03.470
They began this war
to gain control of our organization.

241
00:48:04.350 --> 00:48:07.310
My father would never have done that.

242
00:48:09.830 --> 00:48:12.790
Your father and Curtiga's father

243
00:48:13.390 --> 00:48:17.590
went to the house of a guy who
had been a friend until the day before.

244
00:48:18.750 --> 00:48:22.230
They killed his wife
and his 7-year-old daughter.

245
00:48:22.310 --> 00:48:26.910
- These are just rumors.
- I had no choice. Stefano.

246
00:48:28.750 --> 00:48:34.390
- My father was a gentleman.
- It was the only way to end the war.

247
00:48:35.750 --> 00:48:37.270
He was your son.

248
00:48:38.950 --> 00:48:40.510
He was your blood!

249
00:48:46.870 --> 00:48:48.870
It broke my heart.

250
00:48:49.430 --> 00:48:52.830
but I had to do it
for the good of all the families.

251
00:48:56.910 --> 00:48:59.350
At least now you know the truth.

252
00:49:23.630 --> 00:49:25.830
Don't touch my wife or my son.

253
00:49:52.190 --> 00:49:53.590
Nicola?

254
00:49:54.310 --> 00:49:55.510
Keep moving.

255
00:50:04.190 --> 00:50:06.070
Wait! Nicola!

256
00:50:06.590 --> 00:50:10.510
- Let me go!
- Stay here. Don't move.

257
00:50:18.190 --> 00:50:21.510
Stefano. come here!
You left me alone!

258
00:50:21.750 --> 00:50:24.030
You piece of shit!

259
00:50:32.790 --> 00:50:35.350
You left me alone!

260
00:50:36.870 --> 00:50:40.790
- You left me all alone!
- I can't come. Nicola!

261
00:50:40.990 --> 00:50:44.150
- Stefano. come here!
- I can't.

262
00:50:44.910 --> 00:50:46.310
I can't...

263
00:50:59.270 --> 00:51:00.790
Sorry. Nicola.

264
00:51:18.230 --> 00:51:21.630
The last thing I wanted
in my life was a war.

265
00:51:23.230 --> 00:51:25.910
But now you're bringing it to me.

266
00:51:28.070 --> 00:51:31.750
I'll win this war. Stefano.

267
00:51:34.950 --> 00:51:38.630
After your father died.
I went into hiding.

268
00:51:39.870 --> 00:51:43.910
You were the one
I missed more than anyone.

269
00:51:45.030 --> 00:51:47.310
You were the age your son is now.

270
00:51:48.910 --> 00:51:50.350
Stefano...

271
00:51:52.230 --> 00:51:54.470
I don't want to do to you

272
00:51:55.310 --> 00:51:57.750
what I once did to your father.

273
00:51:59.790 --> 00:52:01.750
You have to choose. Stefano.

274
00:52:04.430 --> 00:52:06.870
Choose which side to take.

275
00:52:13.270 --> 00:52:15.510
You won't get another chance.

276
00:52:16.790 --> 00:52:20.630
Try to move beyond hatred. Stefano.

277
00:54:20.190 --> 00:54:21.550
Who is it?

278
00:54:36.710 --> 00:54:38.150
Franco!

279
00:54:39.310 --> 00:54:40.790
This way.

280
00:54:47.270 --> 00:54:48.670
Go. go!

281
00:54:56.470 --> 00:54:57.750
Go!

282
00:55:16.230 --> 00:55:17.630
Stefano!

283
00:55:21.790 --> 00:55:24.230
- They know everything.
- What happened?

284
00:55:27.030 --> 00:55:30.270
He killed Nicola
right before my eyes!

285
00:55:30.870 --> 00:55:34.150
- Where the fuck's he heading?
- We need to go after him.

286
00:55:34.510 --> 00:55:36.790
Lift him up or he'll bleed out!
Let's go!

287
00:55:37.305 --> 00:56:37.290
